  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Hii Mission Technologies obligated $1.2B in FY2026 to date across 96 awards, producing an average award size of $12.2M. Year over year obligations are up 0.8%. The General Services Administration is the dominant buyer, accounting for $958M of obligations, followed by the Department of Defense with $210M. Engineering Services and All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services are the largest NAICS markets, with obligations of $508M and $611M respectively. Fiscal-year history shows obligations of $596M in FY21, $657M in FY22, $595M in FY23, $1.1B in FY24, and $1.2B in FY25. Smaller agency buyers include the Department of the Interior at $443K, the Department of Education at $388K, the Department of Homeland Security at $18.8K, and the Department of Commerce at $4K. Industry-specific work includes Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing at $30.7M and Ship Building and Repairing at $12.4M. Current-year totals are partial and reflect fiscal year to date activity.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are the biggest federal buyers of Hii Mission Technologies?",
        "body": "The General Services Administration obligated $958M to Hii Mission Technologies in FY2026 to date. The Department of Defense obligated $210M. The Department of the Interior, Department of Education, Department of Homeland Security, and Department of Commerce follow with $443K, $388K, $18.8K, and $4K respectively."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What markets and services account for Hii Mission Technologies' obligations?",
        "body": "All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services is the largest market with $611M in obligations. Engineering Services follows with $508M. Other notable markets include Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing at $30.7M, Ship Building and Repairing at $12.4M, and Other Support Activities for Air Transportation at $12.2M."
      }
    ]
  },
