      "q": "How much does Hii Mission Technologies make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "Hii Mission Technologies made $1.2B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The company received 96 awards with an average award size of $12.2M, and obligations are up 0.8% year over year."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies buy from Hii Mission Technologies?",
      "a": "The General Services Administration is the largest buyer, obligating $958M to Hii Mission Technologies. The Department of Defense is the next-largest buyer at $210M, with smaller buyers including the Department of the Interior at $443K, the Department of Education at $388K, the Department of Homeland Security at $18.8K, and the Department of Commerce at $4K."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Hii Mission Technologies sell to the government?",
      "a": "Hii Mission Technologies sells work classified mainly as All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services and Engineering Services, with obligations of $611M and $508M respectively. The company also provides Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing ($30.7M), Ship Building and Repairing ($12.4M), and Other Support Activities for Air Transportation ($12.2M), among other services."
